    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Replaces the hardcoded-0 `CommunicationAssessedSignal.Confidence` with a computed score that GATES the shipped notification path (`CommunicationRiActionService` — Task + appnotification + ping). A wrong score either floods users with noise or leaves the path dark. BFF-touching + `.cs` in shared `Services/Communication/` + best-effort non-fatal → code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5; publish-size + CVE + `/conflict-check` required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>P2-triage</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>A well-specified scorer (urgency × rung-agreement blend) wired into a known emission point, with weights tuned against an eval set. Clear inputs/outputs, no open-ended architecture. Default execution tier at `high` effort.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <fr-refs>FR-04</fr-refs>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Compute a real email-specific RI-confidence and pass it into `CommunicationAssessedSignal`, replacing the hardcoded `0` that currently leaves the shipped notification path inert. Today `CommunicationAssessedSignal.Confidence` is hardcoded 0, so `CommunicationRuleGate` denies under any threshold and `CommunicationRiActionService` creates nothing — Pillar 1 stays dark. This task lights it up.

    1. **Compute the score** — an email-specific blend of **triage urgency** (from the triage output / classification signal, task 022/023) **× deterministic-rung agreement** (how strongly the association rungs, incl. task 020's identifier rung, agree on the match). Do NOT reuse the Workspace/Portfolio priority scorer (D-08 — email-specific). The exact weights are tuned during implementation against an eval set (C-5) — start from the spec's urgency × rung-agreement blend and tune so a high-urgency well-associated email scores ≥ the rule-gate threshold and noise scores below it.
    2. **Wire into `CommunicationAssessedSignal`** — set the computed value where `RunAssessmentEmissionAsync` (~L238 in `CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs`) emits the signal, replacing the hardcoded 0. Reading the deterministic-rung agreement uses task 020's rung output (the rung-level/agreement signal); reading urgency uses the triage/classification signal (022/023).
    3. **Light up the notification path** — with a real score, a high-signal email passes `CommunicationRuleGate` and fires `CommunicationRiActionService` (Task + appnotification + real-time ping); noise does not (success-criterion 5). Do NOT modify the shipped gate/action-service behavior beyond feeding the real confidence — the path already exists.
    4. **Best-effort (NFR-04)** — a scorer failure MUST NOT fail the capture/enrichment path; degrade to a safe low/neutral confidence + log, never throw.

    Add tests proving the blend + the gate outcome (high-signal fires, noise does not) + non-fatal degradation. Tune weights against an eval set; record the chosen weights + threshold rationale in the task note.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication enrichment + notification path. Authority on `CommunicationEnrichmentService.RunAssessmentEmissionAsync`, `CommunicationAssessedSignal`, `CommunicationRuleGate`, and `CommunicationRiActionService`. Fluent in the D-08 email-specific scorer decision (do NOT reuse portfolio scoring), the C-5 tune-with-eval-set approach, NFR-04 non-fatal discipline, §10 BFF Hygiene, and the shipped notification spine (feed it a real confidence; do not fork it).
  </role>

  <goal>
    `CommunicationAssessedSignal.Confidence` carries a computed email-specific RI-confidence (urgency × deterministic-rung agreement) set at the `RunAssessmentEmissionAsync` emission point, replacing the hardcoded 0. A high-urgency, well-associated email scores ≥ the rule-gate threshold and fires the shipped `CommunicationRiActionService` (Task + appnotification + ping); noise scores below and fires nothing. The scorer is best-effort (a failure degrades to a safe low/neutral confidence, never throws). Weights + threshold are tuned against an eval set and documented. Build clean; tests prove the blend + gate outcome + non-fatal degradation; existing enrichment/notification tests stay green; publish-size delta ≈0 + no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The notification spine (`CommunicationRiActionService` + `ICommunicationAssessedProducer` + `CommunicationRuleGate`) shipped, but `CommunicationAssessedSignal.Confidence` is hardcoded 0 — so the gate denies under any threshold and the action service creates nothing (spec §New-Components: "notification path stays dark"). FR-04 computes a real email-specific confidence from triage urgency × deterministic-rung agreement and feeds it into the signal, unblocking the shipped path. This is the fix that makes Pillar 1 fire (success-criterion 5).

      §11: this task ONLY modifies existing files (the scorer wires into `CommunicationEnrichmentService`; it replaces a hardcoded value and may add a small scorer helper). The scorer helper, if a new small class, is justified: (1) no existing email-specific RI scorer exists (the hardcoded 0 is the placeholder); (2) the Workspace/Portfolio scorer is explicitly NOT reused (D-08 — different intent, email-specific); (3) without it the notification path stays dark (success-criterion 5 fails). Keep it minimal — a helper on the enrichment path, not a new service surface.

      The exact weights are a C-5 tuning item (spec Assumptions) — tuned with an eval set during implementation, not a blocker. Reads task 020's rung agreement + task 022/023's urgency signal.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationEnrichmentService.cs (`RunAssessmentEmissionAsync` ~L238 — the emission point to set the computed confidence)</file>
