  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` + spec FR-04/D-08/C-5 + `CommunicationEnrichmentService.RunAssessmentEmissionAsync` + `ICommunicationAssessedProducer` + `CommunicationRuleGate` + `CommunicationRiActionService` to fix the emission point, the hardcoded-0 location, the threshold, and the urgency + rung-agreement signal sources.</step>
    <step order="2">Characterize the current inert path with a green baseline (confidence 0 → gate denies → no action) so the fix is a deliberate, tested change.</step>
    <step order="3">Implement the email-specific scorer (urgency × deterministic-rung agreement; NOT the portfolio scorer); read urgency via the classification/triage signal (facade if AI) + rung agreement via task 020's rung output; best-effort (failure → safe low/neutral).</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the computed value into `CommunicationAssessedSignal` at `RunAssessmentEmissionAsync` (~L238), replacing the hardcoded 0; do NOT alter the gate/action-service behavior.</step>
    <step order="5">Tune the weights + threshold against an eval set so high-urgency well-associated emails score ≥ threshold and noise scores below; record the chosen weights + rationale in `notes/024-ri-confidence.md`.</step>
    <step order="6">Add tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/`: (a) a high-signal email scores ≥ threshold and fires `CommunicationRiActionService` (Task + appnotification + ping); (b) NEGATIVE — noise scores below threshold and fires nothing; (c) NEGATIVE — a scorer failure degrades to a safe low/neutral confidence and does NOT throw into capture/enrichment (NFR-04); (d) the score is email-specific (not the portfolio scorer).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build` + `dotnet test --filter Communication`; confirm existing enrichment/notification tests stay green.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release ... -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expected ≈0).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` (focus: email-specific blend not portfolio; feeds not forks the gate/action; best-effort non-fatal; facade for AI signals); `adr-check` (FR-04, D-08, ADR-013, ADR-047, NFR-04). Address Critical findings; cite Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/`; serial within P2-triage — never concurrent with 023/025).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (024 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record the chosen weights, threshold, and the eval-set outcome.</step>
  </steps>

